// ADR-020 / #239 POSITIVE acceptance fixture — the STAGE-StringJIT surface.
//
// A scalar-returning method on a proven `string` receiver whole-function-deopts
// at mir_compiler/terminators.rs:601. That deopt's own message states this
// ticket's thesis: the `jit_call_method` VM trampoline "boxes the scalar result
// via `box_number(.. as f64)` ... NEITHER of which is the raw native scalar the
// proven destination slot expects."
//
// Correct on both tiers today because the function runs interpreted. As with
// the DateTime fixture, VM==JIT is NOT the acceptance assertion — native
// execution is. After the conversion `stringlen` must dispatch natively, which
// is what proves the channel carries a raw typed scalar rather than a renamed
// untyped one.
fn stringlen(s: string) -> int {
    return s.length()
}

fn indexof(s: string) -> int {
    return s.indexOf("l")
}

print(stringlen("hello"))
print(indexof("hello"))
